      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "- PyTorch official documentation & tutorials (pytorch.org/tutorials) — canonical reference for training loops, autograd, and torch_xla/device placement\n- Hugging Face documentation & courses (huggingface.co/docs, huggingface.co/learn) — transformers, datasets, and the free NLP/LLM course\n- Made With ML (madewithml.com) — free, widely-used course on production ML engineering: MLOps, testing, and deployment practices\n- Full Stack Deep Learning (fullstackdeeplearning.com) — course and reading materials on the practical engineering side of shipping ML systems\n- \"Machine Learning Engineering\" by Andriy Burkov (mlebook.com) — concise, practitioner-focused complement to more academic ML texts\n- Google's \"Rules of Machine Learning\" (developers.google.com/machine-learning/guides/rules-of-ml) — battle-tested heuristics from Google's internal ML practice\n- \"Retrieval-Augmented Generation for Knowledge-Intensive NLP Tasks\" (Lewis et al., 2020, arXiv:2005.11401) — the original RAG paper defining the architecture pattern\n- LangChain official documentation (python.langchain.com) — reference patterns for RAG pipelines and agentic tool-calling workflows\n- Awesome MLOps (github.com/visenger/awesome-mlops) — curated, community-maintained list of MLOps tools, papers, and platforms",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "- PyTorch official documentation & tutorials (pytorch.org/tutorials) — canonical reference for training loops, autograd, and torch_xla/device placement\n- Hugging Face documentation & courses (huggingface.co/docs, huggingface.co/learn) — transformers, datasets, and the free NLP/LLM course\n- Made With ML (madewithml.com) — free, widely-used course on production ML engineering: MLOps, testing, and deployment practices\n- Full Stack Deep Learning (fullstackdeeplearning.com) — course and reading materials on the practical engineering side of shipping ML systems\n- \"Machine Learning Engineering\" by Andriy Burkov (mlebook.com) — concise, practitioner-focused complement to more academic ML texts\n- Google's \"Rules of Machine Learning\" (developers.google.com/machine-learning/guides/rules-of-ml) — battle-tested heuristics from Google's internal ML practice\n- \"Retrieval-Augmented Generation for Knowledge-Intensive NLP Tasks\" (Lewis et al., 2020, arXiv:2005.11401) — the original RAG paper defining the architecture pattern\n- LangChain official documentation (python.langchain.com) — reference patterns for RAG pipelines and agentic tool-calling workflows\n- Awesome MLOps (github.com/visenger/awesome-mlops) — curated, community-maintained list of MLOps tools, papers, and platforms",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "index": "aS"
